{
  "title": "[dynamo] KeyError in resume function creation in Python 3.11+",
  "issue_id": "162313",
  "bug_description": "Minimal repro:\n\n```python\nimport torch\n\nflag = True\n\n\n@torch.compile(backend=\"eager\")\ndef fn(x):\n    x = x + 1\n    torch._dynamo.graph_break()\n    x = x + 2\n    if flag:\n        with torch.no_grad():\n            torch._dynamo.graph_break()\n    else:\n        with torch.no_grad():\n            torch._dynamo.graph_break()\n    return x + 4\n\n\nfn(torch.ones(3))\nflag = False\nfn(torch.ones(3))\n```\n\nThis is because we're incorrectly using `meta.block_target_offset_remap` in resume_execution.py.\n\nInternal xref: [T236677438](https://www.internalfb.com/intern/tasks/?t=236677438)\n\ncc @chauhang @penguinwu @voznesenskym @EikanWang @jgong5 @Guobing-Chen @XiaobingSuper @zhuhaozhe @blzheng @wenzhe-nrv @jiayisunx @chenyang78 @kadeng @amjames @Lucaskabela",
